Description: NEXUS Arsenal profile - Reverse Engineering
 Static and dynamic analysis of binaries, libraries, firmware and mobile apps:
 debuggers, decompilers, tracers, hex editors, ELF/PE inspection, emulation
 and fuzzing. For malware analysis, run samples only inside an isolated lab
 (see the lab-setup guide). Ghidra, radare2 and Cutter are not in Debian main
 and are listed as external tools with install links.
 .
 This metapackage recommends the 23 tools of the profile, all from Debian
 main; APT installs them with it. A tool can be removed again without removing
 the profile.
 .
 Not included, because they are not in Debian main: Ghidra, radare2 / Cutter,
 Frida. The Arsenal manager lists where their vendors publish them.
 .
 These tools are for authorised security testing, research, defence and
 education only: use them on systems you own or have explicit written
 permission to test, and follow the law that applies to you. They come with no
 warranty.

